    "dispatch_counts_identical": true,
    "verdict": "IT IS THE SAME NON-GEMV SET AS DECODE. Prefill and decode each dispatch 964 kernels and the harness labels the prefill phase through the same step function. The acceptance asks for same-or-different WITH EVIDENCE, and the evidence is identical dispatch count across a shared code path.",
    "what_this_evidence_is_NOT": "a name-by-name diff. The harness exposes a dispatch COUNT per phase, not a per-kernel name census per phase, so 'identical set' rests on count identity plus the shared code path rather than on comparing 964 names against 964 names.",
    "the_first_step_costs_more_and_it_is_not_the_kernel_set": "The prefill step's GPU time is 55.9 ms against a decode step's ~29.3, and its encode is 2.26 ms against 0.73. That is the COLD first step -- first command buffer, cold caches -- not a different kernel set, and the steady prefill rate measured in G118 is 31.6-39.0 ms/token, not 55.9."
  },
