  "the_shape_of_it": "Post-batching the per-position prefill cost is amortized_base + (N/2)*5.5218 us. Batching amortizes the weight sweep; it does NOT touch the attention over the growing prefix, because that work is per-position by construction. So the attention term is the entire post-batching wall at long context.",
  "crossover": "At 6,989 tokens (optimistic 2.57x batching: 4,433) the attention term equals the ENTIRE amortized weight sweep. Beyond that, prefill is an attention problem and batching is irrelevant to it.",
  "and_it_is_the_same_mechanism_as_decode": "G060 measured the decode context slope at 6.971 us/token and the attention path at 253x its per-element cost; G118 measured the prefill slope at 5.5218 us. The post-batching prefill wall and the decode context wall are the SAME kernel being slow, seen in two phases.",
  "commit": "c30470e40ccbf880bc786ce160c7a72b66565841"
}
